Information Resource Center (hereinafter referred to as IRC) being one of the major structural divisions of Azerbaijan State Marine Academy, is a center providing information support to ASMA’s education and research activities. It is also used as a center furnishing the research process with teaching, scientific, methodological literature and information data,  and disseminating cultural, moral and intellectual supplementary materials.

IRC was created by the order of ADDA No. 1247/K dated 09.09.2015.

IRC, as a center that can be measured for its multifaceted activities, performs its work in different sectors.

The sector operates in accordance with the law of the Republic of Azerbaijan “On access to information” in order to ensure information strategy, press and advertising policy, proper coordination and effective management of Public Relations of the university satisfy the public needs for information in relation to ASMA, and protect and develop the transparent image of the Academy.

In its work IRC is governed by the Constitution of the Republic of Azerbaijan, the law of the Republic of Azerbaijan “On Education”, the law of the Republic of Azerbaijan “On access to information”, the law “On library work”, the orders, decrees and normative documents of the Ministry of Education, as well as by the orders, decrees, and provisions of the Azerbaijan Caspian Shipping Company and Azerbaijan State Marine Academy.

